;; FALSIFICATION TEST for the rerank-truncation hypothesis.
;;
;; Pool-head + rerank-score instrumentation (2026-06-02) found: 20/21 buried-golden
;; runs are a RERANKER miss (golden IS in ColBERT's top-40 window but scored below
;; generic chunks), and 20/20 of those goldens are LONGER than rerank-max-chunk-length
;; (1000). Hypothesis: ColBERT truncates each chunk to its first 1000 chars before
;; late-interaction scoring, so the answer-bearing content of long goldens (median
;; 2440) is truncated away — the reranker scores the golden's generic intro and
;; shorter generic chunks out-score it. This explains why every ADDITIVE/boost lever
;; failed: the golden is retrieved and in-window; the loss is at rerank-time.
;;
;; Test: raise rerank-max-chunk-length 1000 -> 4000 (covers the long goldens). If the
;; long goldens surface (recall@20 up, golden rerank-score up, pool-rank into top-20),
;; truncation is CAUSAL. If not, length was only a correlate. judge? false — the
;; immediate signal is retrieval (does the long golden surface), which doesn't need
;; the judge. 2 × 10 × 3 = 60 runs. Cohort = the 10 retrieval-variance questions.
{:configs
 [{:id "chunklen-1000" :skill-graph-id :builtin/agent-rag-graph-bundled :skill-params {}}
  {:id "chunklen-4000" :skill-graph-id :builtin/agent-rag-graph-bundled
   :skill-params {:builtin/retrieval {:rerank-max-chunk-length 4000}}}]
 :repeats 3
 :judge? false
 :order :interleaved
 :max-clarification-rounds 1
 :run-timeout-ms 300000
 :execution-scope {:tenant "digdir" :dataset-config-key "default" :agent-id "builtin/agent-rag-agent"}
